<title>UK: UK retail sales rise strong one pct in August.</title>
<headline>UK retail sales rise strong one pct in August.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retail sales rose one percent in August for a 4.4 percent annual rise, official data showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The figures were much stronger than analysts had expected and government bonds fell as hopes for a cut in interest rates faded. In July, retail sales had fallen 0.6 percent for a 2.4 percent year-on-year rise.</p>
</text>
